      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Important Sessions of the Indian National Congress"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The administration of British India transitioned from East India Company control under Governor-Generals (1773–1858) to direct British Crown control under Viceroys (1858–1947).",
        "The Indian National Congress was founded in 1885, establishing a platform for annual national political sessions across India.",
        "The Regulating Act of 1773 created the office of Governor-General of Bengal, which evolved into Governor-General of India with the Charter Act of 1833.",
        "The Government of India Act 1858 formally introduced the title of Viceroy of India to represent the British monarch directly."
      ],
      "id": "9q4tswb"
    },
